{"version":3,"term":{"cols":80,"rows":24},"timestamp":1789095344,"command":"sh -c \"printf '$ %s\\\\n' \\\"git why \\\\\\\"when was HTTP/3 support first introduced\\\\\\\" --first\\\"; git why \\\"when was HTTP/3 support first introduced\\\" --first\"","env":{"SHELL":"/bin/zsh"}}
[0.013, "o", "$ git why \"when was HTTP/3 support first introduced\" --first\r\n"]
[5.104, "o", "introduced: 3af0e76  HTTP3: initial (experimental) support  2019-07-21  (by http3)\r\n\r\n1. 011788f  msh3: fix the QUIC disconnect function\r\n   2022-08-12 · Daniel Stenberg\r\n\r\n   And free request related memory better in 'done'. Fixes a memory-leak.\r\n\r\n   Reported-by: Gisle Vanem\r\n   Fixes #8915\r\n   Closes #9304\r\n\r\n   (summary only; no evidence retained for this result)\r\n\r\n2. 026840e  CURLOPT_HTTP_VERSION: seting this to 3 forces HTTP/3 use directly\r\n   2019-08-08 · Daniel Stenberg\r\n\r\n   Even though it cannot fall-back to a lower HTTP version automatically. The\r\n   safer way to upgrade remains via CURLOPT_ALTSVC.\r\n\r\n   CURLOPT_H3 no longer has any bits that do anything and might be removed\r\n   before we remove…\r\n\r\n   docs/libcurl/opts/CURLOPT_HTTP_VERSION.3\r\n    prior knowledge that the server supports HTTP/2 straight away. HTTPS requests\r\n    will still do HTTP/2 the standard way with negotiated protocol version in the\r\n    TLS handshake. (Added in 7.49.0)\r\n   +.IP CURL_HTTP_VERSION_3\r\n   +(Added in 7.66.0)"]
[0.002, "o", " Setting this value will make libcurl attempt to use HTTP/3\r\n   +directly to server given in the URL. Note that this cannot gracefully\r\n   +downgrade to earlier HTTP version if the server doesn't support HTTP/3.\r\n   +\r\n   +For more reliably upgrading into HTTP/3, set the prefered version to something\r\n   +lower and let the server announce its HTTP/3 support via Alt-Svc:. See\r\n   +\\fICURLOPT_ALTSVC(3)\\fP.\r\n    .SH DEFAULT\r\n    Since curl 7.62.0: CURL_HTTP_VERSION_2TLS\r\n    \r\n\r\n   include/curl/curl.h\r\n      CURL_HTTP_VERSION_2TLS, /* use version 2 for HTTPS, version 1.1 for HTTP */\r\n      CURL_HTTP_VERSION_2_PRIOR_KNOWLEDGE,  /* please use HTTP 2 without HTTP/1.1\r\n                                               Upgrade */\r\n   -  CURL_HTTP_VERSION_3 = 30, /* This cannot be set with CURLOPT_HTTP_VERSION,\r\n   -                               use CURLOPT_H3 and/or CURLOPT_ALTSVC to enable\r\n   -                               HTTP/3 */\r\n   +  CURL_HTTP_VERSION_3 = 30, /* Makes use of explicit HTTP/3 without fallback.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "   +                               Use CURLOPT_ALTSVC to enable HTTP/3 upgrade */\r\n      CURL_HTTP_VERSION_LAST /* *ILLEGAL* http version */\r\n    };\r\n    \r\n\r\n3. 0736ee7  vquic: add support for GnuTLS backend of ngtcp2\r\n   2020-03-31 · Daiki Ueno\r\n\r\n   Currently, the TLS backend used by vquic/ngtcp2.c is selected at compile\r\n   time. Therefore OpenSSL support needs to be explicitly disabled.\r\n\r\n   Signed-off-by: Daiki Ueno <dueno@redhat.com>\r\n   Closes #5148\r\n\r\n   configure.ac\r\n    dnl **********************************************************************\r\n    dnl Check for nghttp3 (HTTP/3 with ngtcp2)\r\n    dnl **********************************************************************\r\n\r\n4. 084404b  CURLOPT_H3: removed\r\n   2019-08-09 · Daniel Stenberg\r\n\r\n   There's no use for this anymore and it was never in a release.\r\n\r\n   Closes #4206\r\n\r\n   docs/libcurl/opts/CURLOPT_HTTP_VERSION.3\r\n    directly to server given in the URL. Note that this cannot gracefully\r\n    downgrade to earlier HTTP version if the server do"]
[0.001, "o", "esn't support HTTP/3.\r\n    \r\n   -For more reliably upgrading into HTTP/3, set the prefered version to something\r\n   +For more reliably upgrading to HTTP/3, set the prefered version to something\r\n    lower and let the server announce its HTTP/3 support via Alt-Svc:. See\r\n    \\fICURLOPT_ALTSVC(3)\\fP.\r\n    .SH DEFAULT\r\n\r\n5. 088c08a  ngtcp2: add CURLOPT_SSL_CTX_FUNCTION support for openssl+wolfssl\r\n   2023-01-10 · Stefan Eissing\r\n\r\n   Using common method for SSL_CTX initialization of verfiy peer and CA\r\n   settings. This also provides X509_STORE sharing to become available for\r\n   ngtcp2+openssl HTTP/3.\r\n\r\n   Reported-by: violetlige on github\r\n\r\n   Fixes #10222\r\n   C…\r\n\r\n   lib/vtls/openssl.c\r\n      }\r\n    #endif\r\n    \r\n   -  result = set_up_x509_store(cf, data, backend);\r\n   +  result = Curl_ssl_setup_x509_store(cf, data, backend->ctx);\r\n      if(result)\r\n        return result;\r\n    \r\n"]
